<title>USA: Riviera Holdings Corp Q1 net declines. [CORRECTED 19:07 GMT]</title>
<headline>Riviera Holdings Corp Q1 net declines. [CORRECTED 19:07 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Month Period Ended March 31</p>
<p>					($ in 000s)</p>
<p>						 1997		    1996</p>
<p>					(Unaudited)</p>
<p> Net revenues			    39,478		  41,723</p>
<p> EBITDA				     7,506		   8,431</p>
<p> Income from operations		 5,073		   6,543</p>
<p> Interest expense		     (3,013)		 (3,061)</p>
<p> Income before taxes		    1,507		   3,759</p>
<p> Net income				   979		   2,473</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	   5,220		   5,048</p>
<p> Fully diluted earnings per share    0.19		    0.49</p>
<p>NOTE - The company reported net income of $979,000, or 19 cents per share. Net income was impacted by an $850,000 charge against earnings for the postponed secondary offering. Without this one-time charge, net income for the quarter would have been $1.5 million (corrects from $1.8 million), or 29 cents per share (corrects from 35 cents per share).</p>
<p>For the first quarter of 1996, net revenues were $41.7 million and net income was $2.5 million or 49 cents per share.</p>
</text>
